\newlabel{tab:abl_a1}{{4}{8}{Ablation A1 ($\times 4$): prototype query refine. PSNR(dB)/SSIM (Y channel) at iter 80k and block-averaged normalized prototype-usage entropy on Urban100. Enabling refine gives the better reconstruction on both benchmarks under the short finetune protocol; it is retained as it improves (and does not degrade) quality while keeping slot assignment stable}{table.caption.31}{}}
\newlabel{tab:abl_a1@cref}{{[table][4][]4}{[1][8][]8}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Ablation A2 ($\times 4$): incremental confidence-aware routing components. PSNR(dB)/SSIM (Y channel) at iter 80k. The full configuration (v4) attains the best reconstruction, but the intermediate steps are not monotone; under the short finetune protocol the components are mutually compatible and quality-preserving rather than individually accuracy-additive.}}{8}{table.caption.32}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:abl_a2}{{5}{8}{Ablation A2 ($\times 4$): incremental confidence-aware routing components. PSNR(dB)/SSIM (Y channel) at iter 80k. The full configuration (v4) attains the best reconstruction, but the intermediate steps are not monotone; under the short finetune protocol the components are mutually compatible and quality-preserving rather than individually accuracy-additive}{table.caption.32}{}}
